# Your Own Design

You can create a custom sign‑in page instead of the default one.

Create `pages/auth/signin.js`. Inside, use `signIn('github')` to trigger GitHub OAuth directly, or render a form for credentials.

Then update the NextAuth options:

```js
export const authOptions = {
  pages: {
    signIn: '/auth/signin',
  },
};
```

Now every time NextAuth needs a sign‑in, it'll route to your page.

slides.codeSnippet:
// pages/auth/signin.js
import { getProviders, signIn } from 'next-auth/react';

export default function SignIn({ providers }) {
  return (
    <div>
      <h1>Welcome Back</h1>
      {Object.values(providers).map(provider => (
        <div key={provider.name}>
          <button onClick={() => signIn(provider.id)}>
            Sign in with {provider.name}
          </button>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  );
}

export async function getServerSideProps() {
  const providers = await getProviders();
  return { props: { providers } };
}

slides.content:
Wrap your app in `<SessionProvider>` in `_app.js` to make the session available to all components. Then `useSession` works everywhere.

```jsx
import { SessionProvider } from 'next-auth/react';

export default function App({ Component, pageProps: { session, ...pageProps } }) {
  return (
    <SessionProvider session={session}>
      <Component {...pageProps} />
    </SessionProvider>
  );
}
```
